From 64d54f85ac2d837edafd517f369867e4da7424ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:05:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a password input shows a mask and edits its value

An input of type password keeps its value beside the editor, which holds
a bullet (U+2022) for each character instead. Each edit of the mask is
made to the value too: an edit replaces the selection, or deletes a run
beside a collapsed one, with what it inserts before the caret, so the
old selection, the lengths and the caret give the range and the text.
The input event, form submission and TextInputData::value carry the
value; the value attribute sets it. As in a browser, the value is not
copied or cut, the field composes nothing (an IME's commit still types),
and a change of type to or from password masks it or shows it again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
